1
00:00:04,030 --> 00:00:07,290
So...couldn't help but notice

2
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:10,990
none of you RSVP'd to my murder mystery dinner party.

3
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:12,260
Oh, yeah.

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:13,770
We were meaning to do that.

5
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:15,350
No, you weren't, because it was a week ago

6
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:17,470
and nobody came!

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,450
So, if you want to solve the mystery of who stabbed

8
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:22,140
Koothrappali in the back with the weapon of indifference,

9
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:24,150
it was all of you.

10
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,870
I don't think that qualifies as a mystery.

11
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:28,960
We all knew what we were doing.

12
00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:32,240
We're sorry, Rajesh.

13
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,720
Maybe we can do it next week.

14
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,350
Whoa, whoa, we're not that sorry.

15
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:37,990
Don't worry, I can take a hint.

16
00:00:37,990 --> 00:00:40,000
No more murder mystery parties.

17
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,560
- Thank you. - Hallelujah.

18
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:43,430
Because I've got something even better planned.

19
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:44,760
- Aw! Why? - Come on.

20
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:46,260
Just hear me out.

21
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:47,460
I'm going to make you guys

22
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:51,360
a scavenger hunt like they have at M.I.T.

23
00:00:51,570 --> 00:00:52,520
I loved those.

24
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:53,890
I did them every year there.

25
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:55,430
We did them at Princeton, too.

26
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:58,120
Oh, that's cute. Like it's a real college.

27
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:01,660
That's amusing-- I was going to say that about M.I.T.,

28
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:04,580
but it works for Princeton, too.

29
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:07,110
Scavenger hunts at Harvard were really tough.

30
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:09,080
I always got stuck on the first challenge--

31
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:11,730
trying to find someone to be on a team with me.

32
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:16,310
I guess that story's more sad than funny.

33
00:01:18,030 --> 00:01:19,080
I love scavenger hunts.

34
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,750
My friends and I had them all the time.

35
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:22,150
Oh, these are a little different.

36
00:01:22,150 --> 00:01:24,320
There's a tradition at elite universities.

37
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:25,480
And Princeton.

38
00:01:27,030 --> 00:01:29,010
A tradition of hunts full of puzzles

39
00:01:29,010 --> 00:01:32,680
that rely on logic and obscure knowledge, science.

40
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,300
Oh, in ours we would just run around town

41
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,250
looking for a store that would sell us beer.

42
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:40,200
So, uh, who's in?

43
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,870
- I think it sounds fun. - Yeah, me, too.

44
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:43,730
- I'm in. - Let's do it.

45
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:45,950
I'm sorry. Are we really doing this

46
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:47,500
or are we tricking Koothrappali again

47
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,580
like with the dinner party?

48
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,690
What's all this?

49
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:19,500
Oh, everything I could possibly need

50
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,540
to win the scavenger hunt.

51
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:25,020
You really think he's gonna send us to a bowling alley?

52
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,460
Well, if he does,

53
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:29,300
do you know how filthy those rental balls are?

54
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,210
They might as well stand on the corner

55
00:02:31,210 --> 00:02:33,940
and give away free rectal exams.

56
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:39,330
Okay, everybody.

57
00:02:39,330 --> 00:02:41,900
Who's ready for a...

58
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:46,410
scavenger hunt...?

59
00:03:03,090 --> 00:03:04,310
Somewhere...

60
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:06,650
in the city of Pasadena,

61
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:10,940
I've hidden a golden coin.

62
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:15,080
You will be faced with a total

63
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,740
of ten puzzles!

64
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:21,880
Each p...

65
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:24,390
Each...

66
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:26,610
each puzzle will lead you

67
00:03:26,610 --> 00:03:28,850
to the location of the next.

68
00:03:28,850 --> 00:03:30,220
The last of which

69
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:33,010
will lead you to the coin.

70
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:36,620
The first team that finds it...

71
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:39,960
wins!

72
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:43,780
He is a born showman.

73
00:03:45,130 --> 00:03:48,320
Any questions?

74
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:49,970
Yes, to be fair,

75
00:03:49,970 --> 00:03:52,880
do people who went to Princeton get a head start?

76
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:54,600
That's not funny.

77
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,360
Oh, it actually is if you get the joke.

78
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,680
It's based on the premise

79
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:01,310
that Princeton isn't a very good school.

80
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:02,960
Ha-ha.

81
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:05,040
Oh, see? Now he gets it.

82
00:04:06,270 --> 00:04:07,330
Okay, guys, go ahead

83
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:09,800
and divide yourselves into teams of two.

84
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,140
Should we just do couples?

85
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,010
Couples sounds great.

86
00:04:12,010 --> 00:04:13,930
Or we could mix things up.

87
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:15,670
Maybe pick names out of a hat.

88
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:16,540
Whatever.

89
00:04:19,910 --> 00:04:20,860
Why don't you just admit

90
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:22,860
you don't want to be on a team with me.

91
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:25,180
I just said, "couples sound great."

92
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:26,530
Yeah, you don't think I'm smart enough.

93
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:28,410
You think I'm gonna be a liability.

94
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:29,600
Even though I totally just used

95
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:33,320
the word "liability" correctly in a sentence.

96
00:04:34,490 --> 00:04:36,250
Yeah.

97
00:04:37,050 --> 00:04:37,920
All right, let's-let's do couples.

98
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:38,780
I want to.

99
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:39,920
No, no, no.

100
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,300
Let's mix things up.

101
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:43,740
I choose Sheldon, and we're gonna kick your ass!

102
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:45,890
Yeah... really?

103
00:04:45,890 --> 00:04:47,640
The only time I'm ever picked first for a team

104
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,950
and I'm stuck with the liability?

105
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:53,880
Stop that. Penny is not a liability.

106
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,580
Thank you. Do you want to be on my team?

107
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:58,490
Maybe we pick names out of a hat.

108
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:01,560
All right, hurry up and close the door

109
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,470
so they can't hear us.

110
00:05:08,230 --> 00:05:09,650
Would you stop pouting?

111
00:05:09,650 --> 00:05:10,760
So, you picked my name.

112
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:12,810
Get over it.

113
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:15,070
Yes, and do you know what the odds are

114
00:05:15,070 --> 00:05:17,100
- I'd pick your name? - No.

115
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:19,570
It's not hard-- one in five.

116
00:05:19,570 --> 00:05:21,870
Now you know why I'm pouting.

117
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:24,630
All right, teams.

118
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:27,130
Get ready to open your first puzzle.

119
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:28,570
Go!

120
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:32,360
Do you see what I did?

121
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:34,690
The first puzzle is a puzzle!

122
00:05:34,690 --> 00:05:37,280
Oh, my God, how adorable is that?

123
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:40,720
I wish I had a friend like me.

124
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:43,260
What are you doing?

125
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:44,810
You have to start with the edges.

126
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:45,890
Well, there's no right way, Sheldon.

127
00:05:45,890 --> 00:05:47,630
I already found a few pieces that fit.

128
00:05:47,630 --> 00:05:51,560
Yeah, well, take them apart and start with the edges.

129
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:54,140
And stop wasting time.

130
00:05:55,970 --> 00:05:58,350
Wow, you're really good at puzzles.

131
00:05:58,350 --> 00:06:00,040
I did them all the time as a kid.

132
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,340
As my mom used to say,

133
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:02,440
"When you're doing a puzzle,

134
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:05,110
it's like having a thousand friends."

135
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:10,150
She was full of fun lies like that.

136
00:06:10,150 --> 00:06:10,900
If it makes you feel any better,

137
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:13,320
my mom's just full of pound cake.

138
00:06:14,850 --> 00:06:16,330
I'm sorry you got stuck with me.

139
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:18,750
I bet you wanted to be with Bernadette.

140
00:06:19,090 --> 00:06:21,460
- Have you ever played a game with Bernadette? - No.

141
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:24,990
Have you ever gone into a steel cage with a wolverine?

142
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,300
Faster, faster, faster!

143
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:28,110
Do you not know that word?

144
00:06:28,110 --> 00:06:29,930
It means "more fast"!

145
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:32,440
Stop yelling at me.

146
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,430
Hey!

147
00:06:33,430 --> 00:06:36,480
You'll know when I'm yelling at you.

148
00:06:36,930 --> 00:06:38,530
Ooh, ooh, it's the comic book store!

149
00:06:38,530 --> 00:06:39,290
All right, come on.

150
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:40,370
That's where we have to go.

151
00:06:40,370 --> 00:06:42,560
But we haven't finished the puzzle.

152
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,430
Well, it-it doesn't matter!

153
00:06:44,430 --> 00:06:45,770
We know the answer! Come on.

154
00:06:45,770 --> 00:06:47,860
You think you know the answer.

155
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:49,390
But it could be a trick.

156
00:06:49,390 --> 00:06:51,290
What if when the puzzle's complete,

157
00:06:51,290 --> 00:06:53,070
there's a sign in the window that says,

158
00:06:53,070 --> 00:06:55,530
"Go to the train store"?

159
00:06:55,810 --> 00:06:57,030
Okay, it's not gonna say that.

160
00:06:57,030 --> 00:06:58,650
Well, I hope you're wrong.

161
00:06:58,650 --> 00:07:01,640
I really want to go to the train store.

162
00:07:02,810 --> 00:07:03,790
It's the comic book store.

163
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:04,920
Let's go!

164
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:06,510
Come on, numb nuts,

165
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:08,210
it's the comic book store!

166
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:17,010
It's the comic book store, it's the comic book store,

167
00:07:17,010 --> 00:07:19,260
it's the comic book store!

168
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,750
It's the comic book store.

169
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:39,220
Do you think Penny's mad at me?

170
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:40,610
Because you're in the right lane behind a bus

171
00:07:40,610 --> 00:07:41,570
and you won't go around it?

172
00:07:41,570 --> 00:07:43,850
I'm sure she finds it charming.

173
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:47,320
No, because I didn't want her on my team.

174
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:49,610
I'm starting to think she dodged a bullet.

175
00:07:49,610 --> 00:07:52,390
The slowest bullet in the world.

176
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:56,510
Geez, I never realized you were so competitive.

177
00:07:56,930 --> 00:07:58,060
Yeah, I know.

178
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,520
It's-it's probably because I grew up

179
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:00,970
with five brothers and sisters

180
00:08:00,970 --> 00:08:02,140
so I had to fight for every...

181
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:04,800
Oh, my God, you did not just slow down for a bird!

182
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:07,220
You know they fly, right?!

183
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,720
I think this is the first time we've ever

184
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,700
actually been alone together.

185
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:18,340
Huh, I guess you're right.

186
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,010
Wonder why that is?

187
00:08:20,010 --> 00:08:21,190
Well, off the top of my head,

188
00:08:21,190 --> 00:08:22,750
I'd say we don't have a lot in common

189
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:24,940
except for the people we're involved with.

190
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,080
Plus, when we first met,

191
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:29,420
Penny warned me never to get into a car alone with you.

192
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,510
Yeah.

193
00:08:34,130 --> 00:08:38,020
You know, I bet you and I have more in common than we think.

194
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:39,700
Such as?

195
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:41,150
I don't know.

196
00:08:41,150 --> 00:08:42,540
Tell me some things you like.

197
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:43,820
Uh, let's see.

198
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:47,290
I like harps, Little House on the Prairie,

199
00:08:47,290 --> 00:08:49,390
medieval poetry, medieval literature...

200
00:08:49,390 --> 00:08:51,360
Hey, how about some music?

201
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:53,430
Great.

202
00:08:53,430 --> 00:08:55,590
Sheldon never lets me listen to music in the car.

203
00:08:55,590 --> 00:08:58,290
He doesn't want to be mistaken for a gang member.

204
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:01,270
Find something you like.

205
00:09:01,270 --> 00:09:03,520
Beatles, boring.

206
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:05,890
Eminem, scary.

207
00:09:05,890 --> 00:09:06,630
Weird Al?

208
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:09,110
How old are you?

209
00:09:10,070 --> 00:09:11,510
Neil Diamond?

210
00:09:11,510 --> 00:09:14,100
Yeah, I love Neil Diamond.

211
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:16,580
I love Neil Diamond.

212
00:09:19,470 --> 00:09:22,300
* Sweet Caroline *

213
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:27,320
* Good times never seemed so good *

214
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:30,350
* So good, so good, so good *

215
00:09:30,350 --> 00:09:32,150
* I've been... *

216
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,610
Oh, hey, thanks for letting me use the comic book store

217
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:39,010
as part of the scavenger hunt.

218
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:39,830
Oh, my pleasure.

219
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:41,770
Always happy to help out with fun things

220
00:09:41,770 --> 00:09:44,330
that I wasn't invited to be a part of.

221
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,820
Oh, congratulations.

222
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:48,590
You're the first team to arrive.

223
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:51,130
Yes! It's not a ruse to make fun of me.

224
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:53,610
It's a real game and I'm winning it!

225
00:09:55,450 --> 00:09:58,680
Your next puzzle is a riddle.

226
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,190
And who better to give it to you

227
00:10:00,190 --> 00:10:03,130
than The Riddler?

228
00:10:03,790 --> 00:10:06,350
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go,

229
00:10:06,350 --> 00:10:08,470
go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

230
00:10:08,470 --> 00:10:09,970
How am I faster than you?

231
00:10:09,970 --> 00:10:13,190
I'm wearing heels and I stopped to take a phone call.

232
00:10:13,850 --> 00:10:15,810
I have asthma.

233
00:10:15,810 --> 00:10:18,080
Back off!

234
00:10:18,590 --> 00:10:19,480
"Riddle me this.

235
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:22,100
"Arrah, Arrah, and gather round,

236
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:25,000
The work of this hero is legion-bound.

237
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:27,420
He multiplies N by the number of He,

238
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:31,390
and in this room the thing you'll see."

239
00:10:31,390 --> 00:10:32,860
- Good riddle, huh? - Yeah.

240
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:34,590
So when you guys plan fun activities,

241
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:35,930
does my name even...

242
00:10:36,590 --> 00:10:38,680
come up, or...?

243
00:10:39,830 --> 00:10:42,300
I invited you to my murder mystery party.

244
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:44,810
No, you didn't.

245
00:10:49,350 --> 00:10:51,040
We're the last ones here, hurry up!

246
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:52,970
It is a marathon, not a sprint.

247
00:10:52,980 --> 00:10:54,150
People run in a marathon!

248
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:56,830
Not with a bowling ball on their back.

249
00:10:57,250 --> 00:10:58,950
Hey, Penny, I just wanted to say good luck,

250
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,350
and I hope there's no hard feelings.

251
00:11:00,350 --> 00:11:01,500
Hey, Romeo!

252
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:04,710
Repair your relationship on your own time.

253
00:11:05,530 --> 00:11:07,050
Relax, it's a hard puzzle.

254
00:11:07,050 --> 00:11:08,430
It's gonna take a while to solve.

255
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:10,210
- "Riddle me this..." - Got it.

256
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:13,410
Hey, Princeton, look at that,

257
00:11:13,410 --> 00:11:16,740
Team Community College Night School is in the lead.

258
00:11:17,490 --> 00:11:20,110
I thought we were the Lightning Sharks.

259
00:11:21,410 --> 00:11:23,320
Hey, you know what this could mean...

260
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:26,010
Oh, oh, that's good.

261
00:11:26,010 --> 00:11:28,190
Then this would be...

262
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:29,600
That's it.

263
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,450
To the Neil Mobile!

264
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:34,820
I knew it, we're gonna lose!

265
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:36,350
Wait, I got it. I got it!

266
00:11:36,350 --> 00:11:39,940
Congratulations, you got it last.

267
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:48,290
You're really mean, you know that?

268
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:57,030
So no one's gonna buy anything.

269
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,090
Okay...

270
00:12:03,090 --> 00:12:04,400
Let's see.

271
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:05,860
"To continue on your quest,

272
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:07,710
leave no stone unturned."

273
